{
  "abstract": "Can a Transformer train without a backward pass—zero pullbacks, VJP helpers, or same-step relays inside `with torch.no_grad():`—while beating matched-subset node perturbation? We study 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) across 133 backward-free multi-seed arms (`exp26`–`exp54`, plus 7 pullback and 15 exact-BP arms; $155$ arms $=464$ runs) on repeatedly inspected `DEV`/`VAL-B` splits over short horizons on ClimbMix `d6` ($L=6,D\\in\\{256..768\\}$, $360$–$1,004$st) and Native `50.3M` ($L=8,D=512,T=2,048$, $100$st). We prove stream-partitioned WM (Prop. 1), commute $W_v$ with attention ($+0.1104\\to+0.9069$ cos, Prop. 2), route lexical credit via a diagonal skip (Prop. 3), bound `RMSNorm` residual by $\\kappa_4(x)/D$ (Prop. 4), and prove the 4th-moment variance drop of reward tangent projection (Prop. 5). Fused Triton cuts `d6` WM time $38.4\\times$ ($134.31\\to3.50$ ms) and step time $8.33\\times$ ($155.6\\to18.68$ ms). On 360st `d6`, 4-mat WM hits $2.0682\\pm0.0006$ `DEV` BPB (vs. $2.0532$ 4-mat BP, $2.2603$ `SR-LNP`, $2.2415$ `SR-NP`); 6-mat $(W_Q,W_K)$ (`99.9978%` active) hits $2.0552\\pm0.0007$ ($M=4$, $60.2\\%$ of BP gain), and at $720$st hits $1.9756\\pm0.0017$ ($M=2$, `21.77s`) and $1.9672\\pm0.0005$ (pure $M=4$, $61.1\\%$ of BP gain). Uniform 6-mat $M=2$ trails extra-step 4-mat WM at equal time ($2.0454$ at $438$st; $1.9720$ at $1,004$st in this trainer), whereas Upper-Half `(3,4,5)` captures $90.1\\%$–$92.9\\%$ of the 720st gain (`1.9779`, `18.59s`), hits $1.9699\\pm0.0001$ ($720$st $M=4$, `21.05s`) and $1.9670\\pm0.0002$ ($740$st $M=4$, `19.19s`), and **beats 1,004st 4-mat WM at matched `~21.6s` same-trainer time ($840$st $M=2$: $1.9609\\pm0.0006$ `DEV`, $1.9264\\pm0.0007$ `VAL-B`, $218.03$ PPL)**. On 100st `50.3M`, isolated Triton speeds up `fwd+rule` $6.33\\times$ ($M_g=1$), hitting $1.8978\\pm0.0007$ (4-mat) and **$1.8853\\pm0.0013$ `DEV` BPB ($201.21$ PPL) on 6-mat $M=2$ ($99.9990\\%$ active)**, trailing 6-mat BP ($1.8904$ on 720st `d6`; $1.6989$ on `50.3M`).",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "1. Executed 8 new 3-seed arms on ClimbMix d6 (24 runs across Seeds 46, 47, 48 in exp53 and exp54; total 155 multi-seed arms = 464 runs): (a) 100% RNG-Stream-Matched 720-Step 2x2 Depth Factorial (exp53 Arm 1): Full 6-Block (0..5) M=2 inside train_d6_exp50_arm (isolated CUDA RNGs matching Lower-Half & Upper-Half) reaches 1.9756 +- 0.0017 DEV BPB (1.9408 +- 0.0019 VAL-B, 226.95 PPL in 21.77s), confirming Upper-Half (3,4,5) M=2 (1.9779 +- 0.0006 in 18.59s) captures 90.1% (-0.0210 / -0.0233 BPB) of the full 6-block gain at half the SDPA probe overhead. (b) Pure M=4 vs. M=4 + ve_gate Isolation at 720 Steps (exp53 Arm 2): Pure 6-matrix M=4 without ve_gate reaches 1.9672 +- 0.0005 DEV BPB (1.9324 +- 0.0005 VAL-B, 221.80 PPL in 27.71s), beating M=4 + ve_gate (1.9683 +- 0.0007 in 28.57s) by -0.0011 +- 0.0007 BPB across all 3 seeds and recovering 61.1% (-0.0317 / -0.0519 BPB) of the 720-step 4-to-6-matrix Exact-BP gain (1.9423 -> 1.8904). (c) Fixed-Probe Upper-Half M=4 Reallocation (exp53 Arm 3 & exp54 Arm 3): Concentrating all 24 SDPA probes/step on Upper-Half (3,4,5) (M=4 on 3,4,5; M=0 on 0,1,2) at fixed 720 steps reaches 1.9699 +- 0.0001 DEV BPB (1.9349 +- 0.0001 VAL-B, 223.42 PPL in 21.05s)—beating uniform 720st Full 6-Block M=2 (1.9756/1.9763) and 1,004st 4-matrix (1.9720 in 21.55s)—and at 740 steps reaches 1.9670 +- 0.0002 DEV BPB (1.9321 +- 0.0002 VAL-B, 221.69 PPL in 19.19s). (d) Stage-2 Bus Multi-Probe (M_bus=2: 1.9699 +- 0.0002) and Compositional Reader Controls (exp53 Arm 4, exp54 Arms 1,2,4: 1.9779-1.9787). 2. Applied all v7 review notes (reconciled Table 5/Sec 4.6 lower-half/long-window rows to 18.90s/17.82s, added same-trainer and descriptive window/RNG qualifications, corrected 438st VAL-B to 2.0092 +- 0.0006).",
